-- The cumulative query of head: head's inverse asks P(head xs <= x) as
-- xs <= x : ANY, and the constant list arm compared it with list equality,
-- so P(X <= 2) for a head that is always 1 came out 0. Lists are ordered
-- componentwise (IRCompiler.Monad.compareValueExpr), so the wildcard tail
-- bounds nothing and the head is compared with <=. The if-spelling of the
-- same distribution (main = if Uniform < 2.0 then 1 else 2) agrees.
-- Task head-cdf-uses-equality.
main = head (if Uniform < 2.0 then [1, 0] else [2])
